{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-60949","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-117127","text":"Floor attribution — what one admitted transition spends its cycles on"}]},{"id":"blk-60950","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117128","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status:"},{"id":"spn-117129","text":" measurement note, opened 2026-09-19. Opens no new semantics, adds no feature to any image, changes no anchor. Its receipts are stamped, not gated. "},{"id":"spn-117130","marks":["bold"],"text":"Instrument:"},{"id":"spn-117131","text":" "},{"id":"spn-117132","marks":["code"],"text":"tools/floor_attribution.py"},{"id":"spn-117133","text":"; it reuses "},{"id":"spn-117134","marks":["code"],"text":"tools/kernellet_abi.py"},{"id":"spn-117135","text":" (ptrace, build), "},{"id":"spn-117136","marks":["code"],"text":"tools/sflr_bench.py"},{"id":"spn-117137","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-117138","marks":["code"],"text":"measure"},{"id":"spn-117139","text":", provenance) and "},{"id":"spn-117140","marks":["code"],"text":"tools/r4_shootout.py"},{"id":"spn-117141","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-117142","marks":["code"],"text":"MixSUT"},{"id":"spn-117143","text":", the BENCHMIX mixes). "},{"id":"spn-117144","marks":["bold"],"text":"Numbers:"},{"id":"spn-117145","text":" "},{"id":"spn-117146","marks":["code"],"text":"receipts/FLOOR-ATTRIBUTION-{SMOKE|OFFICIAL}-<stamp>.{md,json}"},{"id":"spn-117147","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-60951","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117148","text":"No numeral in this document is a measurement."}]},{"id":"blk-60952","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-117149","text":"0. The question, and why it was asked"}]},{"id":"blk-60953","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117150","text":"The compiled WRL backend ("},{"id":"spn-117151","marks":["code"],"text":"TRVM/compiled/"},{"id":"spn-117152","text":") folds a sealed world's epoch as one C step over a few hundred bits, four to six orders of magnitude under the interaction calculus reducing the same epoch. That made a proposal natural: if the world's laws were expressed once at a meta level, discharged at admission over the sealed finite state space, and the step, its residual checks, its battery and its certificate all "},{"id":"spn-117153","marks":["italic"],"text":"generated"},{"id":"spn-117154","text":" from that one source — how much of the floor could go with them?"}]},{"id":"blk-60954","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117155","text":"The proposal's premise is that the floor spends cycles checking world-local law. This note and its tool ask whether that premise is true of "},{"id":"spn-117156","marks":["code"],"text":"cd-kernellet"},{"id":"spn-117157","text":" as built, in two halves:"}]},{"id":"blk-60955","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60957","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117158","marks":["bold"],"text":"By reading"},{"id":"spn-117159","text":" (§2): what does "},{"id":"spn-117160","marks":["code"],"text":"step"},{"id":"spn-117161","text":" check, and is any of it a WRL law?"}]}],"id":"blk-60956","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-60959","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117162","marks":["bold"],"text":"By measuring"},{"id":"spn-117163","text":" (§3): of one transition's cost, how much is the semantic"}]}],"id":"blk-60958","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-60960","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117164","text":"step at all, and how much is carrying a context in and out of it?"}]},{"id":"blk-60961","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117165","text":"Only the first half can say \"none\". The second says what a change to either half would be worth."}]},{"id":"blk-60962","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-117166","text":"1. What a transition is here"}]},{"id":"blk-60963","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117167","text":"The subject is the promoted production floor ("},{"id":"spn-117168","marks":["code"],"text":"prod"},{"id":"spn-117169","text":", no features; R4-P, "},{"id":"spn-117170","marks":["code"],"text":"receipts/R4-P-PROMOTED.md"},{"id":"spn-117171","text":"), whose image anchor the tool checks against the newest "},{"id":"spn-117172","marks":["code"],"text":"receipts/R7-BATTERY-*.json"},{"id":"spn-117173","text":" before it measures anything (F141). One transition is one "},{"id":"spn-117174","marks":["code"],"text":"step(lineage, op, …) -> (lineage, outcome)"},{"id":"spn-117175","text":": "},{"id":"spn-117176","marks":["code"],"text":"kernellet_main"},{"id":"spn-117177","text":" takes the slot's "},{"id":"spn-117178","marks":["code"],"text":"Option<Lineage>"},{"id":"spn-117179","text":" out of "},{"id":"spn-117180","marks":["code"],"text":"TABLE"},{"id":"spn-117181","text":", calls "},{"id":"spn-117182","marks":["code"],"text":"step"},{"id":"spn-117183","text":", and puts the returned lineage back. The lineage is the Locus Core Context — admission, finality warden, possession — and the authority row lives in a private sidecar, borrowed by AUTH and consumed-and-returned by GRANT/REVOKE ("},{"id":"spn-117184","marks":["code"],"text":"authority_store"},{"id":"spn-117185","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-60964","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-117186","text":"2. What "},{"id":"spn-117187","marks":["code"],"text":"step"},{"id":"spn-117188","text":" checks, by line"}]},{"id":"blk-60965","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117189","text":"Every check reached from "},{"id":"spn-117190","marks":["code"],"text":"step"},{"id":"spn-117191","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-117192","marks":["code"],"text":"cd-kernellet/src/main.rs"},{"id":"spn-117193","text":", the "},{"id":"spn-117194","marks":["code"],"text":"step"},{"id":"spn-117195","text":" function) at the promoted default, and what kind of fact it is about:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-60967","spans":[{"id":"spn-117196","text":"op"}]},{"id":"blk-60968","spans":[{"id":"spn-117197","text":"check"}]},{"id":"blk-60969","spans":[{"id":"spn-117198","text":"where"}]},{"id":"blk-60970","spans":[{"id":"spn-117199","text":"kind"}]}],"id":"blk-60966","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-60971","spans":[{"id":"spn-117200","text":"ATTACH"}]},{"id":"blk-60972","spans":[{"id":"spn-117201","text":"possession is "},{"id":"spn-117202","marks":["code"],"text":"Vacant"},{"id":"spn-117203","text":", else "},{"id":"spn-117204","marks":["code"],"text":"BAD_POSSESSION"}]},{"id":"blk-60973","spans":[{"id":"spn-117205","marks":["code"],"text":"step"},{"id":"spn-117206","text":", "},{"id":"spn-117207","marks":["code"],"text":"OP_ATTACH"},{"id":"spn-117208","text":" arm"}]},{"id":"blk-60974","spans":[{"id":"spn-117209","text":"lifecycle state machine"}]}],[{"id":"blk-60975","spans":[{"id":"spn-117210","text":"ATTACH"}]},{"id":"blk-60976","spans":[{"id":"spn-117211","marks":["code"],"text":"adm.locus == self.locus"},{"id":"spn-117212","text":" → else "},{"id":"spn-117213","marks":["code"],"text":"WrongLocus"}]},{"id":"blk-60977","spans":[{"id":"spn-117214","marks":["code"],"text":"cd-core/src/locus.rs"},{"id":"spn-117215","text":" "},{"id":"spn-117216","marks":["code"],"text":"admits"}]},{"id":"blk-60978","spans":[{"id":"spn-117217","text":"provenance"}]}],[{"id":"blk-60979","spans":[{"id":"spn-117218","text":"ATTACH"}]},{"id":"blk-60980","spans":[{"id":"spn-117219","marks":["code"],"text":"adm.mark == self.mark"},{"id":"spn-117220","text":" → else "},{"id":"spn-117221","marks":["code"],"text":"ForeignProvenance"}]},{"id":"blk-60981","spans":[{"id":"spn-117222","marks":["code"],"text":"admits"}]},{"id":"blk-60982","spans":[{"id":"spn-117223","text":"provenance"}]}],[{"id":"blk-60983","spans":[{"id":"spn-117224","text":"ATTACH"}]},{"id":"blk-60984","spans":[{"id":"spn-117225","marks":["code"],"text":"adm.carrier.is_none()"},{"id":"spn-117226","text":" → else "},{"id":"spn-117227","marks":["code"],"text":"NotVacant"}]},{"id":"blk-60985","spans":[{"id":"spn-117228","marks":["code"],"text":"VacantLocus::attach"}]},{"id":"blk-60986","spans":[{"id":"spn-117229","text":"succession"}]}],[{"id":"blk-60987","spans":[{"id":"spn-117230","text":"ATTACH"}]},{"id":"blk-60988","spans":[{"id":"spn-117231","marks":["code"],"text":"adm.generation == self.generation"},{"id":"spn-117232","text":" → else "},{"id":"spn-117233","marks":["code"],"text":"WrongGeneration"}]},{"id":"blk-60989","spans":[{"id":"spn-117234","marks":["code"],"text":"VacantLocus::attach"}]},{"id":"blk-60990","spans":[{"id":"spn-117235","text":"succession"}]}],[{"id":"blk-60991","spans":[{"id":"spn-117236","text":"ATTACH"}]},{"id":"blk-60992","spans":[{"id":"spn-117237","text":"build "},{"id":"spn-117238","marks":["code"],"text":"LocusAttachment"},{"id":"spn-117239","text":", "},{"id":"spn-117240","marks":["code"],"text":"AttachRecord"},{"id":"spn-117241","text":", "},{"id":"spn-117242","marks":["code"],"text":"adm.advanced(...)"}]},{"id":"blk-60993","spans":[{"id":"spn-117243","marks":["code"],"text":"VacantLocus::attach"}]},{"id":"blk-60994","spans":[{"id":"spn-117244","text":"the successor state"}]}],[{"id":"blk-60995","spans":[{"id":"spn-117245","text":"DETACH"}]},{"id":"blk-60996","spans":[{"id":"spn-117246","text":"possession is "},{"id":"spn-117247","marks":["code"],"text":"Attached"},{"id":"spn-117248","text":", else "},{"id":"spn-117249","marks":["code"],"text":"BAD_POSSESSION"}]},{"id":"blk-60997","spans":[{"id":"spn-117250","marks":["code"],"text":"step"},{"id":"spn-117251","text":", "},{"id":"spn-117252","marks":["code"],"text":"OP_DETACH"},{"id":"spn-117253","text":" arm"}]},{"id":"blk-60998","spans":[{"id":"spn-117254","text":"lifecycle state machine"}]}],[{"id":"blk-60999","spans":[{"id":"spn-117255","text":"DETACH"}]},{"id":"blk-61000","spans":[{"id":"spn-117256","marks":["code"],"text":"admits"},{"id":"spn-117257","text":" (locus, mark)"}]},{"id":"blk-61001","spans":[{"id":"spn-117258","marks":["code"],"text":"LocusAttachment::detach"}]},{"id":"blk-61002","spans":[{"id":"spn-117259","text":"provenance"}]}],[{"id":"blk-61003","spans":[{"id":"spn-117260","text":"DETACH"}]},{"id":"blk-61004","spans":[{"id":"spn-117261","marks":["code"],"text":"adm.carrier"},{"id":"spn-117262","text":" is "},{"id":"spn-117263","marks":["code"],"text":"Some"},{"id":"spn-117264","text":" → else "},{"id":"spn-117265","marks":["code"],"text":"NotAttached"}]},{"id":"blk-61005","spans":[{"id":"spn-117266","marks":["code"],"text":"detach"}]},{"id":"blk-61006","spans":[{"id":"spn-117267","text":"succession"}]}],[{"id":"blk-61007","spans":[{"id":"spn-117268","text":"DETACH"}]},{"id":"blk-61008","spans":[{"id":"spn-117269","text":"generation matches → else "},{"id":"spn-117270","marks":["code"],"text":"WrongGeneration"}]},{"id":"blk-61009","spans":[{"id":"spn-117271","marks":["code"],"text":"detach"}]},{"id":"blk-61010","spans":[{"id":"spn-117272","text":"succession"}]}],[{"id":"blk-61011","spans":[{"id":"spn-117273","text":"DETACH"}]},{"id":"blk-61012","spans":[{"id":"spn-117274","marks":["code"],"text":"live == self.carrier"},{"id":"spn-117275","text":" → else "},{"id":"spn-117276","marks":["code"],"text":"WrongCarrier"}]},{"id":"blk-61013","spans":[{"id":"spn-117277","marks":["code"],"text":"detach"}]},{"id":"blk-61014","spans":[{"id":"spn-117278","text":"succession"}]}],[{"id":"blk-61015","spans":[{"id":"spn-117279","text":"DETACH"}]},{"id":"blk-61016","spans":[{"id":"spn-117280","text":"build "},{"id":"spn-117281","marks":["code"],"text":"VacantLocus"},{"id":"spn-117282","text":" (generation + 1), "},{"id":"spn-117283","marks":["code"],"text":"DetachReceipt"},{"id":"spn-117284","text":", "},{"id":"spn-117285","marks":["code"],"text":"adm.advanced(...)"}]},{"id":"blk-61017","spans":[{"id":"spn-117286","marks":["code"],"text":"detach"}]},{"id":"blk-61018","spans":[{"id":"spn-117287","text":"the successor state"}]}],[{"id":"blk-61019","spans":[{"id":"spn-117288","text":"FINALIZE"}]},{"id":"blk-61020","spans":[{"id":"spn-117289","text":"basis code in {0,1,2} → else "},{"id":"spn-117290","marks":["code"],"text":"BAD_BASIS"}]},{"id":"blk-61021","spans":[{"id":"spn-117291","marks":["code"],"text":"step"},{"id":"spn-117292","text":", "},{"id":"spn-117293","marks":["code"],"text":"OP_FINALIZE"},{"id":"spn-117294","text":" arm"}]},{"id":"blk-61022","spans":[{"id":"spn-117295","text":"ABI"}]}],[{"id":"blk-61023","spans":[{"id":"spn-117296","text":"FINALIZE"}]},{"id":"blk-61024","spans":[{"id":"spn-117297","marks":["code"],"text":"admits"},{"id":"spn-117298","text":"; carrier "},{"id":"spn-117299","marks":["code"],"text":"Some"},{"id":"spn-117300","text":"; generation; carrier match"}]},{"id":"blk-61025","spans":[{"id":"spn-117301","marks":["code"],"text":"FinalityWarden::finalize_loss"}]},{"id":"blk-61026","spans":[{"id":"spn-117302","text":"provenance, succession"}]}],[{"id":"blk-61027","spans":[{"id":"spn-117303","text":"FINALIZE"}]},{"id":"blk-61028","spans":[{"id":"spn-117304","marks":["code"],"text":"FencingEpoch { epoch } > fence"},{"id":"spn-117305","text":" → else "},{"id":"spn-117306","marks":["code"],"text":"StaleFencingEpoch"}]},{"id":"blk-61029","spans":[{"id":"spn-117307","marks":["code"],"text":"finalize_loss"}]},{"id":"blk-61030","spans":[{"id":"spn-117308","text":"succession (fencing)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-61031","spans":[{"id":"spn-117309","text":"FINALIZE"}]},{"id":"blk-61032","spans":[{"id":"spn-117310","text":"build "},{"id":"spn-117311","marks":["code"],"text":"LossFinalization"},{"id":"spn-117312","text":", successor "},{"id":"spn-117313","marks":["code"],"text":"VacantLocus"},{"id":"spn-117314","text":", "},{"id":"spn-117315","marks":["code"],"text":"adm.advanced(...)"}]},{"id":"blk-61033","spans":[{"id":"spn-117316","marks":["code"],"text":"finalize_loss"}]},{"id":"blk-61034","spans":[{"id":"spn-117317","text":"the successor state"}]}],[{"id":"blk-61035","spans":[{"id":"spn-117318","text":"STATE"}]},{"id":"blk-61036","spans":[{"id":"spn-117319","text":"nothing: the values are handed back"}]},{"id":"blk-61037","spans":[{"id":"spn-117320","marks":["code"],"text":"step"},{"id":"spn-117321","text":", "},{"id":"spn-117322","marks":["code"],"text":"OP_STATE"},{"id":"spn-117323","text":" arm"}]},{"id":"blk-61038","spans":[{"id":"spn-117324","text":"—"}]}],[{"id":"blk-61039","spans":[{"id":"spn-117325","text":"GRANT / REVOKE"}]},{"id":"blk-61040","spans":[{"id":"spn-117326","text":"row not full → else "},{"id":"spn-117327","marks":["code"],"text":"BAD_EVIDENCE_FULL"},{"id":"spn-117328","text":"; the successor row carries one more stamped entry"}]},{"id":"blk-61041","spans":[{"id":"spn-117329","marks":["code"],"text":"cd-core/src/authority_row.rs"},{"id":"spn-117330","text":" "},{"id":"spn-117331","marks":["code"],"text":"transition"}]},{"id":"blk-61042","spans":[{"id":"spn-117332","text":"authority (evidence)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-61043","spans":[{"id":"spn-117333","text":"AUTH"}]},{"id":"blk-61044","spans":[{"id":"spn-117334","text":"walk the row: last matching grant/revocation for (worker, locus) decides"}]},{"id":"blk-61045","spans":[{"id":"spn-117335","marks":["code"],"text":"cd-core/src/authority.rs"},{"id":"spn-117336","text":" "},{"id":"spn-117337","marks":["code"],"text":"reconstruct"}]},{"id":"blk-61046","spans":[{"id":"spn-117338","text":"authority"}]}],[{"id":"blk-61047","spans":[{"id":"spn-117339","text":"any"}]},{"id":"blk-61048","spans":[{"id":"spn-117340","text":"slot in range, slot in use, world booted"}]},{"id":"blk-61049","spans":[{"id":"spn-117341","marks":["code"],"text":"dispatch"}]},{"id":"blk-61050","spans":[{"id":"spn-117342","text":"ABI / table"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-61051","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117343","marks":["bold"],"text":"Every row is about a locus, a carrier, a generation, a fence epoch, a mark or a worker."},{"id":"spn-117344","text":" Not one is about a WRL object: no spinner saturation, no door's COMMIT-then-REACT, no affine single-use, no width bound. Those are checked in the compiled step's admission battery and in the calculus, not here. The floor's safety is "},{"id":"spn-117345","marks":["italic"],"text":"succession"},{"id":"spn-117346","text":" safety — the same carrier cannot be attached twice, a stale attachment cannot detach, a fence epoch cannot go backwards — and its authority is "},{"id":"spn-117347","marks":["italic"],"text":"evidence"},{"id":"spn-117348","text":" authority. All of it is open-world: it is about who and which and when, none of it about what the world computes."}]},{"id":"blk-61052","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117349","text":"So the strong form of the proposal — \"hoist the WRL laws and the floor shrinks\" — is answered by reading: the floor would shrink by nothing, because it evaluates none of them. What remains is the second half."}]},{"id":"blk-61053","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-117350","text":"3. How the measurement is made"}]},{"id":"blk-61054","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117351","text":"Two instruments over the "},{"id":"spn-117352","marks":["bold"],"text":"same command streams on the same image in the same run"},{"id":"spn-117353","text":", reconciled per row before anything is subtracted:"}]},{"id":"blk-61055","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61057","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117354","marks":["bold"],"text":"perf"},{"id":"spn-117355","text":", R4's instrument: user-domain hardware counters"}]}],"id":"blk-61056","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-61058","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117356","text":"("},{"id":"spn-117357","marks":["code"],"text":"sflr_bench.measure"},{"id":"spn-117358","text":"), marginal between K and 2K iterations of one in-image BENCHMIX command so BOOT, BEGIN, the pre-GRANTs and the I/O loop cancel; median of repeats; a multiplexed reading is dropped, never scaled."}]},{"id":"blk-61059","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61061","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117359","marks":["bold"],"text":"ptrace"},{"id":"spn-117360","text":", R1's instrument: PTRACE_SINGLESTEP over the same streams at"}]}],"id":"blk-61060","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-61062","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117361","text":"small iteration counts, again as a K → 2K difference, every executed rip bucketed by "},{"id":"spn-117362","marks":["bold"],"text":"symbol"},{"id":"spn-117363","text":": inside "},{"id":"spn-117364","marks":["code"],"text":"step"},{"id":"spn-117365","text":", inside "},{"id":"spn-117366","marks":["code"],"text":"memcpy"},{"id":"spn-117367","text":", elsewhere in "},{"id":"spn-117368","marks":["code"],"text":".text"},{"id":"spn-117369","text":". "},{"id":"spn-117370","marks":["code"],"text":"memcpy"},{"id":"spn-117371","text":" entries are counted and their widths read from "},{"id":"spn-117372","marks":["code"],"text":"%rdx"},{"id":"spn-117373","text":" (R4 F66), so bytes moved per op is exact."}]},{"id":"blk-61063","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117374","marks":["code"],"text":"step"},{"id":"spn-117375","text":" is a symbol only in the "},{"id":"spn-117376","marks":["code"],"text":"benchraw"},{"id":"spn-117377","text":" images — "},{"id":"spn-117378","marks":["code"],"text":"prod"},{"id":"spn-117379","text":" inlines it into "},{"id":"spn-117380","marks":["code"],"text":"kernellet_main"},{"id":"spn-117381","text":" — so those are the images traced, in two families: "},{"id":"spn-117382","marks":["code"],"text":"benchraw"},{"id":"spn-117383","text":" (byte-loop intrinsics) and "},{"id":"spn-117384","marks":["code"],"text":"benchraw"},{"id":"spn-117385","text":"+"},{"id":"spn-117386","marks":["code"],"text":"fastmem"},{"id":"spn-117387","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-117388","marks":["code"],"text":"rep movsb"},{"id":"spn-117389","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-117390","marks":["code"],"text":"rep stosb"},{"id":"spn-117391","text":" intrinsics). Both carry the promoted default's semantics exactly; "},{"id":"spn-117392","marks":["code"],"text":"benchraw"},{"id":"spn-117393","text":" is "},{"id":"spn-117394","marks":["code"],"text":"bench"},{"id":"spn-117395","text":" with the rdtsc pair and histogram removed, so nothing that measures is in the loop. M4 holds: each traced image runs the full external witness battery ("},{"id":"spn-117396","marks":["code"],"text":"kernellet_census.battery"},{"id":"spn-117397","text":") first, and a failure blocks its numbers."}]},{"id":"blk-61064","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117398","marks":["bold"],"text":"The control."},{"id":"spn-117399","text":" BENCHMIX mix 3 is "},{"id":"spn-117400","marks":["code"],"text":"STATE, STATE"},{"id":"spn-117401","text":": the lineage is taken from the table, "},{"id":"spn-117402","marks":["code"],"text":"step"},{"id":"spn-117403","text":" is called on an op whose only work is to hand the values back, and the lineage is put back. It is the plumbing of a transition with no semantics in it. For a semantic mix "},{"id":"spn-117404","marks":["italic"],"text":"m"},{"id":"spn-117405","text":", "},{"id":"spn-117406","marks":["code"],"text":"semantic(m) = per_op(m) − per_op(3)"},{"id":"spn-117407","text":", in cycles and in instructions, and the tool refuses the subtraction unless both rows reconciled. The ptrace split gives the same answer a second way: instructions inside "},{"id":"spn-117408","marks":["code"],"text":"step"},{"id":"spn-117409","text":" against instructions outside it."}]},{"id":"blk-61065","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117410","marks":["bold"],"text":"Reconciliation, and the instrument fact it turned up."},{"id":"spn-117411","text":" A "},{"id":"spn-117412","marks":["code"],"text":"rep"},{"id":"spn-117413","text":"-prefixed string instruction retires once under perf but traps once per "},{"id":"spn-117414","marks":["italic"],"text":"iteration"},{"id":"spn-117415","text":" under PTRACE_SINGLESTEP. The tool therefore counts "},{"id":"spn-117416","marks":["italic"],"text":"distinct consecutive rips"},{"id":"spn-117417","text":" as retired-instruction equivalents (no instruction in these images jumps to itself) and prints the iterations in their own column. On "},{"id":"spn-117418","marks":["code"],"text":"fastmem"},{"id":"spn-117419","text":" those iterations are the bytes "},{"id":"spn-117420","marks":["code"],"text":"rep movsb"},{"id":"spn-117421","text":" moved. Inside "},{"id":"spn-117422","marks":["code"],"text":"step"},{"id":"spn-117423","text":" they are an inlined "},{"id":"spn-117424","marks":["code"],"text":"rep movsq"},{"id":"spn-117425","text":" aggregate copy (LLVM's lowering; seven sites inside "},{"id":"spn-117426","marks":["code"],"text":"step"},{"id":"spn-117427","text":") on the FINALIZE and AUTH paths — present in "},{"id":"spn-117428","marks":["italic"],"text":"both"},{"id":"spn-117429","text":" families, and invisible to R1's ptrace-vs-perf agreement check because that check was made on the byte-loop image, where a constant nine-step excess sits under a per-cent tolerance on a thousand-instruction transition. The first version of this tool compared raw steps and passed the byte-loop rows the same way; the fastmem rows, an order of magnitude smaller, exposed it. The reconciliation rule is now one rule for both families: retired-equivalent ptrace count against perf instructions, per op, within a stated tolerance, or the row DISAGREES and is withheld from the split."}]},{"id":"blk-61066","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117430","marks":["bold"],"text":"Two loops over the same pair."},{"id":"spn-117431","text":" "},{"id":"spn-117432","marks":["code"],"text":"bench"},{"id":"spn-117433","text":" (op 20, the loop R1 and R2 published) and mix 0 (op 24) both perform ATTACH then DETACH on each context. The receipt prints each loop's memcpy entries and bytes moved per op so the difference between them — the published figure carries more copies per pair than the mix — is read from the row, not assumed."}]},{"id":"blk-61067","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-117434","text":"4. What the numbers do not say"}]},{"id":"blk-61068","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61070","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117435","text":"Nothing about a WRL law; §2 is the whole answer there, by reading."}]}],"id":"blk-61069","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61072","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117436","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-117437","marks":["code"],"text":"semantic"},{"id":"spn-117438","text":" column is succession, provenance and authority. It is the"}]}],"id":"blk-61071","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-61073","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117439","text":"cost of the floor's own laws, which are also hand-transcribed into the C, Go, Erlang and cd-core comparators ("},{"id":"spn-117440","marks":["code"],"text":"sflr/"},{"id":"spn-117441","text":", "},{"id":"spn-117442","marks":["code"],"text":"fcb/kc/"},{"id":"spn-117443","text":") and cross-checked by the class-S suite — the generator question, if it is asked, is asked of "},{"id":"spn-117444","marks":["italic"],"text":"those"},{"id":"spn-117445","text":" laws."}]},{"id":"blk-61074","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61076","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117446","text":"The mix-3 control's in-"},{"id":"spn-117447","marks":["code"],"text":"step"},{"id":"spn-117448","text":" count is zero because the compiler"}]}],"id":"blk-61075","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-61077","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117449","text":"specialises "},{"id":"spn-117450","marks":["code"],"text":"step"},{"id":"spn-117451","text":" for a constant op and the STATE arm is a move; the control is take + put + the call shape, which is what it is meant to be."}]},{"id":"blk-61078","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61080","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117452","text":"A smoke receipt is taken on a shared host and says so in its status line;"}]}],"id":"blk-61079","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-61081","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117453","text":"the spreads are printed. Only an "},{"id":"spn-117454","marks":["code"],"text":"--official"},{"id":"spn-117455","text":" run under "},{"id":"spn-117456","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/battery-host-profile.md"},{"id":"spn-117457","text":" is evidence."}]},{"id":"blk-61082","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61084","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117458","text":"Nothing is compared across languages here, and nothing here enters the FCB"}]}],"id":"blk-61083","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-61085","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117459","text":"kernellet-cost campaign ("},{"id":"spn-117460","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/fcb-kernellet-cost-contract.md"},{"id":"spn-117461","text":") or the reverse."}]},{"id":"blk-61086","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-61088","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117462","text":"Hardware counters are this CPU, this frequency, this day. Stamped, never"}]}],"id":"blk-61087","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-61089","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-117463","text":"diffed."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaiera7mezooxdn5fhfkk5bap7rdtnd4eypylhgw27ly5kp4zrgbrurwrq","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}